(2866418, 399026, 53316, '<td valign="top">DICE!!!!!!!!!  <br/>*cough cough ahem*  (I''m not a dice geek.. no really.... *cough*)<br/> <br/>I think the problem here is that this is definitely recognizable at first glance.  But... it is recognizable to me.  Most people won''t understand what a d12 is and might see it as meeting the challenge more than I do.  What I may have tried to do is get in closer to the dice so that the edges weren''t as recognizable?  But then you have the problem of context - it might not look like a macro, at that point, because there''s nothing to compare the size of the dice to.  It''s sort of a tough decision but I do think that even for people who don''t recognize d12s, they can see that there is a definite "subject" in your shot, making it less abstract than they might prefer.<br/> <br/><a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=312163" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">My entry</a> in the first Abstract Macro challenge included a d20 and got a really helpful comment from the critique club that you may be interested in looking at.<br/> <br/>I love the colors and the reflections... Your title is great because what really makes this image so great to look at is the rainbow bits.</td>', 'DICE!!!!!!!!!  *cough cough ahem*  (I''m not a dice geek.. no really.... *cough*) I think the problem here is that this is definitely recognizable at first glance.  But... it is recognizable to me.  Most people won''t understand what a d12 is and might see it as meeting the challenge more than I do.  What I may have tried to do is get in closer to the dice so that the edges weren''t as recognizable?  But then you have the problem of context - it might not look like a macro, at that point, because there''s nothing to compare the size of the dice to.  It''s sort of a tough decision but I do think that even for people who don''t recognize d12s, they can see that there is a definite "subject" in your shot, making it less abstract than they might prefer. My entry in the first Abstract Macro challenge included a d20 and got a really helpful comment from the critique club that you may be interested in looking at. I love the colors and the reflections... Your title is great because what really makes this image so great to look at is the rainbow bits.', '2006-09-26 16:00:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2866422, 400685, 30049, '<td valign="top">You didn''t go out a buy a new set of pencils just for this challenge - did you?  ;^)  Just pulling your leg, been there, done that myself.  This is a good choice of subject for the challenge.  A bit static and maybe a little short on the "wow" factor - but it should do "ok".  I think an even tighter framing with 8 full ends showing might have had more impact.  Anyway, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'You didn''t go out a buy a new set of pencils just for this challenge - did you?  ;^)  Just pulling your leg, been there, done that myself.  This is a good choice of subject for the challenge.  A bit static and maybe a little short on the "wow" factor - but it should do "ok".  I think an even tighter framing with 8 full ends showing might have had more impact.  Anyway, good luck in the challenge.', '2006-09-26 16:00:26.000000', NULL, 1),
