(2886024, 400128, 36377, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen a lot of these abstract water shots, but this is in the top 3 if not the best I''ve seen. Nice work.</td>', 'I''ve seen a lot of these abstract water shots, but this is in the top 3 if not the best I''ve seen. Nice work.', '2006-10-02 04:51:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2886029, 400565, 60165, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by B74A:</b></div><hr/><i> Looking forward to hear about shutter, aperture and ISO etc for this one ... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Haha, I have a camera just like it, and have tried the same! The zero-inch super macro is aaaawesome in this camera, but the problem is often the light, as the lens starts to block it up close.<br/> <br/>Hint for future uses: Put camera lens up, towards (a not too bright sky), set manual focus to zero, and now you can put various items direclt on the lens and get amazing shots this way. One other interesting thing to try with this amazing and versatile camera is the time lapse function. Put it on a tripod, set it to 50 shots, every 5 minutes, and watch the world go by. Microsoft movie maker (free) can make the shots into a time lapsed video clip ...</td>', 'Originally posted by B74A: Looking forward to hear about shutter, aperture and ISO etc for this one ...   Haha, I have a camera just like it, and have tried the same! The zero-inch super macro is aaaawesome in this camera, but the problem is often the light, as the lens starts to block it up close. Hint for future uses: Put camera lens up, towards (a not too bright sky), set manual focus to zero, and now you can put various items direclt on the lens and get amazing shots this way. One other interesting thing to try with this amazing and versatile camera is the time lapse function. Put it on a tripod, set it to 50 shots, every 5 minutes, and watch the world go by. Microsoft movie maker (free) can make the shots into a time lapsed video clip ...', '2006-10-02 04:59:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2886036, 400915, 54778, '<td valign="top">woohooo!!! u did it..finally got a ribbon and a blue one at that. Great Job!!</td>', 'woohooo!!! u did it..finally got a ribbon and a blue one at that. Great Job!!', '2006-10-02 05:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2886038, 400754, 18552, '<td valign="top">What a nice picture, Irene - it is very abstract and even though it''s red (a hot color) it is very relaxing to look at it. The curves are really soothing. I''m glad it did well for you!</td>', 'What a nice picture, Irene - it is very abstract and even though it''s red (a hot color) it is very relaxing to look at it. The curves are really soothing. I''m glad it did well for you!', '2006-10-02 05:15:50.000000', NULL, 0),
