(2937448, 398996, 59215, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ambaker:</b></div><hr/><i> Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>I don''t know if there was a way to emphasize the distortions, that some saw as marks, in the glass.  If they were more pronounced you could see the top of the picture as connected to the blue in a sort of tornado effect.  Otherwise, it might have been better to clone them out.  (Permissable in this challenge as it is advanced editing.) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi and thanks for the review. I was thinking more on this point as well and maybe could have brought out that line/distortion more with some creative dodging.</td>', 'Originally posted by ambaker: Critique Club Review: I don''t know if there was a way to emphasize the distortions, that some saw as marks, in the glass.  If they were more pronounced you could see the top of the picture as connected to the blue in a sort of tornado effect.  Otherwise, it might have been better to clone them out.  (Permissable in this challenge as it is advanced editing.)   Hi and thanks for the review. I was thinking more on this point as well and maybe could have brought out that line/distortion more with some creative dodging.', '2006-10-17 19:29:27.000000', NULL, 0),
